#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0483 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "[STALE MECHANISM, corrected 2026-08-27] NonEmptyGuardInliner was DELETED (Fix #367 / EC-100) and no guard is injected at load any more; the expectation below still holds, but for the rule's AUTHORED Requirements/Check, not for the injection this note describes. THE 82-RULE GENERATOR-WILDCARD POPULATION (Fix #331 finding; owner ruled 2026-08-22 that all 82 are BUCKET 1 - no rule edit - with a sample of fixtures owed by the closing lane; authored by Fix #340). These rules never carried the injected var_exists guard in rules/ (NonEmptyGuardInliner.isGeneratorWildcard excludes wildcard names), but WildcardExpander re-ran installNativeExpr on the EXPANDED rule, where the arm wrapped the now-concrete leaf - so before Fix #330 an absent primary column silenced them at runtime. With the arm retired the expanded leaf is a bare empty(X): absent = all-missing, TRUE on every row. The mirror: the SECONDARY column BCHGCA1N is absent. The y=1 tuple is raised off the declared BCHGCAT1 and not empty(BCHGCA1N) is FALSE on every row of an absent column, so the rule is correctly silent."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID    type=Char
col USUBJID    type=Char
col PARAMCD    type=Char
col BCHGCAT1   type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | GLUC | WORSENED
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | GLUC |
